<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:45:45 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns after affair raises national security concerns</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-to-step-down-after-affair</link><description>
Nvidia announced on Thursday that CEO Jensen Huang was stepping down following revelations that he had an affair with a woman accused of spying for China. The company's chief financial officer Colette Kress will serve as interim CEO while the board searches for Huang's successor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7e5a9ba-dea0-11f1-b255-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T115845Z-1141769569-RC2I6KAPBYZ3-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-CEO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7e5a9ba-dea0-11f1-b255-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T115845Z-1141769569-RC2I6KAPBYZ3-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-CEO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a527a7cc-dea1-11f1-91f0-af0225855907</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:06:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7e5a9ba-dea0-11f1-b255-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T115845Z-1141769569-RC2I6KAPBYZ3-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-CEO.jpg">© Carlos Barria, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>China accuses US of 'fabricating' Nvidia spy claims to push tech 'blockade'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261112-china-accuses-us-fabricating-nvidia-spy-claims-to-push-tech-blockade</link><description>
China on Thursday accused the United States of “fabricating spy narratives” to justify a technology “blockade”, stepping up its pushback against reports that the woman Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang had an affair with was a Chinese intelligence asset. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06ebee50-de70-11f1-9d44-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D76L3LZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06ebee50-de70-11f1-9d44-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D76L3LZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">17cab916-de72-11f1-81bc-652a33ff1cd0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:40:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06ebee50-de70-11f1-9d44-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D76L3LZ.jpg">© Idrees Mohammed, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Undone by a honey trap? Nvidia's Jensen Huang at heart of China spy scandal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261111-undone-by-a-honey-trap-nvidia-s-jensen-huang-at-heart-of-china-spy-scandal</link><description>
It turns out that the new masters of the universe are human – all too human. Nvidia co-founder Jensen Huang has admitted to an extramarital affair with Singapore-based Chinese tech CEO Alice Huang, who is no relation. She's under scrutiny over the purchase of Nvidia state-of-the-art chips that may have been smuggled back to the mainland illegally.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72346862-de03-11f1-b9d6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T025315Z-781474958-RC2BKOASZBEJ-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-PROBE-CEO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/72346862-de03-11f1-b9d6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T025315Z-781474958-RC2BKOASZBEJ-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-PROBE-CEO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a8454b0-de03-11f1-be99-658c0699aa0d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:32:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>AI, affair and espionage: Why is Nvidia's chief Jensen Huang under scrutiny?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-ai-affair-and-espionage-why-is-nvidia-s-chief-jensen-huang-under-scrutiny</link><description>
Nvidia chief and tech titan Jensen Huang was in the spotlight on Monday after acknowledging an affair with a woman US officials say was working for Chinese intelligence, a claim Beijing denied. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8cd174a-dc2d-11f1-91f1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1-4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8cd174a-dc2d-11f1-91f1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1-4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">152246fc-dc2e-11f1-a711-f5910a563915</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 11:45:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Diwali: Over one billion people mark victory of light over darkness</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness</link><description>
Diwali celebrations began on Sunday, with people across India and the global diaspora gathering to mark one of the most important festivals in the Hindu tradition. In Ayodhya, believed to be the birthplace of Lord Rama, the deity celebrated during the festival, festivities included performances based on the Hindu epic Ramayana, laser and light shows, live music, fireworks and drone displays.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cac0a34c-db60-11f1-b422-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111252-111423-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cac0a34c-db60-11f1-b422-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111252-111423-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cfba9c7c-db60-11f1-9841-59074deecd2b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:46:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>New Zealand's knife-edge parliamentary election delivers no clear winner</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261108-new-zealand-election-produces-no-clear-winner-as-smaller-parties-make-record-gains</link><description>
No clear winner was produced in New Zealand’s legislative elections Saturday, setting up the two main blocs – Prime Minister Christopher Luxon's right-wing coalition and opposition leader Chris Hipkins' left-wing alliance – for weeks of political wrangling to attempt to cobble together a majority. Hipkins said that while New Zealanders had spoken, "it may take us a little bit longer to figure out exactly what it is that you've said".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c039f738-db20-11f1-a5eb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/c7f3463382f4a345e7ea10396c4211fa925e0888.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c039f738-db20-11f1-a5eb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/c7f3463382f4a345e7ea10396c4211fa925e0888.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c0f7dc58-db20-11f1-b17a-bb43f820a77d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 03:01:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c039f738-db20-11f1-a5eb-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/c7f3463382f4a345e7ea10396c4211fa925e0888.jpg">© Ben Strang, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>China keeps a close eye on US midterm shake-up</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261106-china-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-shake-up</link><description>
The US midterm elections have resulted in the Democratic Party taking control of both chambers of the US Congress, leaving Donald Trump as a lame duck president for the remainder of his term. Professor Steve Tsang of the SOAS China Institute tells FRANCE 24 that, while a weakened Trump could strengthen Beijing's negotiating position, the Chinese leadership is aware that Congress has relatively little sway over foreign policy and is keen to maintain warm personal ties between the two presidents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12d8854c-d9da-11f1-a55a-c728c64c10de</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 15:03:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Pollution, shortages, crime: Daily life in Pakistan's megacity Karachi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261106-pollution-shortages-crime-daily-life-in-pakistan-s-megacity-karachi</link><description>
Fed up with hours of power cuts, the residents of Pakistan's economic hub Karachi took to the streets in recent days and blocked several major roads. The outburst of anger highlights the daily problems faced by a megacity of over 21 million people, which has once again been ranked among the world's least liveable cities. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/365618b2-d940-11f1-a61a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-PAKISTAN-KARACHI-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/365618b2-d940-11f1-a61a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-PAKISTAN-KARACHI-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6b376da-d941-11f1-afa8-414edc499c13</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:32:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sonia GHEZALI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Myanmar: Civilians under fire from military junta</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-myanmar-civilians-under-fire-from-military-junta</link><description>
More than five years after the military coup, the junta launched a new offensive in September to retake Rakhine State, intensifying airstrikes against civilians and employing double-tap strikes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d99418a-d870-11f1-bc85-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Arakan-army-bridge.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d99418a-d870-11f1-bc85-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Arakan-army-bridge.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a552602-d920-11f1-8af6-71bde6a42c7d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 17:58:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d99418a-d870-11f1-bc85-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Arakan-army-bridge.png">© Telegram / @AA Info Desk</source><dc:creator>Marguerite MARAMICI</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hong Kong activist jailed for 10 more years for collusion with foreign forces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-hong-kong-activist-jailed-for-10-more-years-for-collusion-with-foreign-forces</link><description>
Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in jail on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, the second time he has been penalised under the city's national security law. Hong, 30, is one of the most globally recognised faces of Hong Kong's pro-democracy movement and has already spent almost six years behind bars. He is now not due for release until late 2036. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1765b516-d909-11f1-8349-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T035351Z-666263956-RC2FHOAZ50XS-RTRMADP-3-HONGKONG-SECURITY-JOSHUAWONG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1765b516-d909-11f1-8349-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-05T035351Z-666263956-RC2FHOAZ50XS-RTRMADP-3-HONGKONG-SECURITY-JOSHUAWONG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e393b208-d906-11f1-8c4e-05f2c72170b2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 11:29:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong gets 10 more years in jail for foreign collusion</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-joshua-wong-hong-kong-10-years-jail-foreign-collusion</link><description>
Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong was sentenced to 10 more years in prison on Thursday for colluding with foreign powers, a court summary said. Wong, 30, pleaded guilty in September to seeking foreign sanctions against Hong Kong and China under Beijing’s national security law, having spent nearly six years imprisoned.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac80546-d89c-11f1-8ab0-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/a3febbc244aae5c0e71fa2e37cf9f5a49bf1acb0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac80546-d89c-11f1-8ab0-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/a3febbc244aae5c0e71fa2e37cf9f5a49bf1acb0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16c3581a-d8c9-11f1-a120-9f5dcb84c312</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 03:31:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bac80546-d89c-11f1-8ab0-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/a3febbc244aae5c0e71fa2e37cf9f5a49bf1acb0.jpg">© Alastair Pike, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>South Korea to deploy military mission to keep Strait of Hormuz open</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261105-south-korea-military-mission-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
South Korea will deploy maritime patrol aircraft and an explosive ordnance disposal team near the Strait of Hormuz to help keep the waterway open, its defence ministry said Thursday. Seoul said it would protect commercial shipping and energy supplies while ruling out military intervention in the ongoing US-Iran war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0048f40-c016-11f1-b91d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/99ebe76c25b49d6da267803d0e58260a8db5112b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0048f40-c016-11f1-b91d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/99ebe76c25b49d6da267803d0e58260a8db5112b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f98789a8-d8bc-11f1-929a-db85ee62d1c5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 02:17:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d0048f40-c016-11f1-b91d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/99ebe76c25b49d6da267803d0e58260a8db5112b.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>How Chinese AI is censoring the controversy around Mbappé’s Chairman Mao comments</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261104-how-chinese-ai-is-censoring-the-controversy-around-mbappes-chairman-mao-comments</link><description>
Footballer Kylian Mbappé sparked a wave of condemnation across China when he implied that Chinese leader Mao Zedong was a dictator. In China, information about this controversy is being censored by Chinese AI chatbots.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47481808-d479-11f1-a1f0-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/image3-137.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47481808-d479-11f1-a1f0-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/image3-137.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63846cdc-d876-11f1-b1b2-c9a7ebac9622</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 20:28:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47481808-d479-11f1-a1f0-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/image3-137.jpg">© Deepseek, Doubao, The Observers, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>South Korea pushes digital detox for young people addicted to screens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261104-south-korea-pushes-digital-detox-for-young-people-addicted-to-screens</link><description>
Back in August, France's Constitutional Council overturned a social media ban for children under 15. Some students, though, are now banned from using their smartphones at school. In South Korea, where an estimated 40 percent of young children and teens are addicted to their mobile devices, authorities are trying to find ways to drastically reduce their screen time – a huge challenge in such a hyper-connected society. FRANCE 24's Chloé Borgnon, Aruna Popuri and Justin McCurry report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c2c6448-d79e-11f1-947f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-SOUTH-KOREA-SCREEN-ADDICTS-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c2c6448-d79e-11f1-947f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-SOUTH-KOREA-SCREEN-ADDICTS-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42aa5d46-d79f-11f1-9a0b-81941c4fc434</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 11:14:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Chloé BORGNON</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>North Korea rejects US allegations over $6 billion Binance crypto heist</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-north-korea-rejects-us-allegations-over-6-billion-binance-crypto-heist</link><description>
North Korea on Tuesday dismissed US allegations that it was behind a $6 billion cryptocurrency theft from Binance as "absurd rhetoric", accusing Washington of seeking to portray the country as a cybercriminal state and warning that US hostility could affect future diplomatic engagement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f8ad8a0-cdb0-11f1-9dd8-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T042855Z-1116982708-RC2SYNASEWEO-RTRMADP-3-NORTHKOREA-SOUTHKOREA-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f8ad8a0-cdb0-11f1-9dd8-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T042855Z-1116982708-RC2SYNASEWEO-RTRMADP-3-NORTHKOREA-SOUTHKOREA-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">008923a2-d718-11f1-9b4c-999dd8670832</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 23:49:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f8ad8a0-cdb0-11f1-9dd8-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T042855Z-1116982708-RC2SYNASEWEO-RTRMADP-3-NORTHKOREA-SOUTHKOREA-1.jpg">© Jorge Silva, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Football: China refuses to air Real Madrid game after Mbappé comment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-football-china-refuses-to-air-real-madrid-game-after-mbapp%C3%A9-comment</link><description>
Chinese state broadcaster CCTV did not broadcast a Real Madrid La Liga match on Sunday after star forward Kylian Mbappé caused a furore in China with remarks he made about former leader Mao Zedong. FRANCE 24's correspondent Jan Camenzind Broomby reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cf76aa84-d6a7-11f1-aa3e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1556c218.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cf76aa84-d6a7-11f1-aa3e-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1556c218.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58839a40-d6a7-11f1-9b94-6f663697c0af</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 11:09:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Taliban voices 'serious concern' over US plan to deport Afghan migrants via Pakistan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261102-taliban-voice-alarm-over-us-plan-to-deport-afghan-migrants-via-pakistan</link><description>
Afghanistan's Taliban government expressed concern on Monday over reported US plans to deport more than 150 Afghans from the US to Pakistan for an eventual return home, with advocacy groups warning the removal could endanger their lives. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/398d5d28-d68a-11f1-ad9d-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253664741444.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/398d5d28-d68a-11f1-ad9d-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253664741444.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d11d446-d68a-11f1-be35-57c13159d13c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 07:26:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/398d5d28-d68a-11f1-ad9d-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253664741444.jpg">© Felix Marquez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Thousands join Indian opposition protest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-join-indian-opposition-protest</link><description>
India’s opposition parties staged major protests in New Delhi on Sunday against Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government and a nationwide voter list review that has fuelled demonstrations since the summer, led by the youth movement Cockroach Janta Party. Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cbb2c10-d61b-11f1-a32b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-170121-170312-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cbb2c10-d61b-11f1-a32b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-170121-170312-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41b35b02-d61b-11f1-bc47-5d108f2cb387</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:45:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Indian opposition parties stage mega rally seeking election chief’s resignation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261101-india-tightens-security-as-opposition-holds-mega-rally-demanding-election-chief-s-resignation</link><description>
